 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Residual-Proxy Adaptive Selector
-An adaptive LOD selection method that uses residual proxies to recover quality over fixed threshold methods at comparable primitive counts [S2, unofficial]. On the 'garden' scene, it recovers 0.49 dB over the fixed threshold at a comparable primitive count (1.05x) [S2, unofficial]. On city-scale models, it exhibits a wider near-lossless window because the aerial model is already tessellated at its training viewing distance, exhausting sub-pixel redundancy at small compression factors ($c$), leaving surplus in super-pixel collapse [S2, unofficial].
+An adaptive LOD selection method that uses residual proxies to recover quality over fixed threshold methods at comparable primitive counts [S2, unofficial]. On the 'garden' scene, it recovers 0.49 dB over the fixed threshold at a comparable primitive count (1.05×) [S2, unofficial]. On city-scale models, it renders 68% of the primitives at −0.05 dB loss with compression factor $c=4$ [S2, unofficial]. The city-scale model exhibits a wider near-lossless window than the garden model because the aerial model is already tessellated at its training viewing distance, exhausting sub-pixel redundancy at small $c$ and leaving surplus in super-pixel collapse [S2, unofficial].
 
